{
  "title": "[RFC] Cuda support matrix for Release 2.9",
  "issue_id": "159980",
  "bug_description": "### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\nUpdate as of Sept 9, 2025:\nWill be including CUDA aarch64 builds for CUDA 12.6, 12.8 and 13.0 and publishing these on download.pytorch.org\n\n\nUpdate as of Aug 18, 2025. Please see the following dev Discuss post: https://dev-discuss.pytorch.org/t/addition-of-cuda-13-0-nightly-builds-and-deprecation-cuda-12-9-builds/3209\n\n\nSimilar to https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/154257\n\nRelated to: https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/159779\n\nOpening this RFC to discuss CUDA version support for future PyTorch release 2.9:\n\nMigration to CUDA 13.0 is planned for release 2.9\n\nHence following few options possible:\n\nOption 1 - CUDA 12.8 (Stable) , 12.9.1 and 13.0 \nCUDA 12.8 CUDNN 9.x - Stable version - Version Release to Pypi \nCUDA 12.9.1 CUDNN 9.x  - Prototype version \nCUDA 13.0 CUDNN 9.x   - Prototype version\n\nOption 2 - CUDA 12.8 and 12.9.1 (Stable) and 13.0 - Requirement here is to be able to move all Pytorch CI to 12.9.1\nCUDA 12.8 CUDNN 9.x - Legacy\nCUDA 12.9.1 CUDNN 9.x  - Stable version - Version Release to Pypi \nCUDA 13.0 CUDNN 9.x   - Prototype version\n\nOption 3 - 12.9.1 (Stable)  and 13.0 - Requirement here is to be able to move all Pytorch CI to 12.9.1\nCUDA 12.9.1 CUDNN 9.x  - Stable version - Version Release to Pypi \nCUDA 13.0 CUDNN 9.x   - Prototype version\n\nOption 4 - 12.8 (Stable)  and 13.0 \nCUDA 12.8 CUDNN 9.x  - Stable version - Version Release to Pypi \nCUDA 13.0 CUDNN 9.x   - Prototype version\n\nOption 5 - CUDA 12.6 CUDA 12.8 (Stable)  and 13.0 \nCUDA 12.6 CUDNN 9.x - Legacy\nCUDA 12.8 CUDNN 9.x - Stable version - Version Release to Pypi \nCUDA 13.0 CUDNN 9.x   - Prototype version\n\nOption 6 - CUDA 12.6 CUDA 12.9 (Stable)  and 13.0 - Requirement here is to be able to move all Pytorch CI to 12.9.1\nCUDA 12.6 CUDNN 9.x - Legacy\nCUDA 12.9 CUDNN 9.x - Stable version - Version Release to Pypi \nCUDA 13.0 CUDNN 9.x   - Prototype version\n\ncc @ptrblck @malfet @nWEIdia @tinglvv @Skylion007 @albanD @ngimel @eqy \n\n### Versions\n\n2.9.0",
